2	//! in-process through jj-lib (the jj-lib migration stage of
3	//! `notes/refactor-20260716.md`).
4	//!
5	//! Reads resolve through `common::load_repo` +
6	//! `common::resolve_revset` and `Commit` accessors; a revset that
7	//! references a working copy (`@`, `@-`, `ws@`) snapshots first
8	//! (`repo_for_read`), so "right now" questions answer about the
9	//! filesystem the way the spawned CLI's auto-snapshot did.
10	//! Mutations run on the `engine` module's settings / snapshot /
11	//! transaction-finish plumbing.
12	//!
13	//! - `matches` / `rev_exists`: does a revset match / does a
14	//!   revision resolve.
15	//! - `chid_of` / `cid_of` / `cid_short_of` / `cids_short_of`:
16	//!   change / commit ids.
17	//! - `desc_of` / `is_empty`: description and emptiness.
18	//! - `is_no_such_revision`: the typed unresolvable-revision test.
19	//! - `commit` / `describe` / `bookmark_set` / `git_push_bookmark` /
20	//!   `git_fetch`: the publish-path mutations.
21	//!
22	//! Still spawning `jj` elsewhere: `bookmark_list` /
23	//! `bookmark_list_all` here (their consumers parse the CLI listing
24	//! textually), and the call sites outside the five verbs
25	//! (`jj squash`, `jj new`, `jj rebase`, `jj op log` / `op restore`,
26	//! `jj git clone`, `jj diff --stat`, repo-init plumbing).
